%I A307185 #20 Sep 25 2026 17:24:59
%S A307185 1,4,65,1993,91454,5539121
%N A307185 The number of level-n generators for phylogenetic networks.
%C A307185 a(5) = 91454 is stated on Gambette's Generators page. It can be checked against his published DOT files: Lev4Gen.txt contains 2063 = 1 + 4 + 65 + 1993 generators of levels 1 through 4, and Lev5Gen.txt contains 93517 of levels 1 through 5, so the level-5 count is 93517 - 2063 = 91454. - _Tyler Satchel Orden_, Aug 07 2026
%C A307185 Every level-(k+1) generator arises from a level-k generator by one of the two rules R1 and R2 of Gambette, Berry and Paul (2009), so the generators of level k+1 can be enumerated from those of level k. - _Tyler Satchel Orden_, Sep 12 2026
%H A307185 Philippe Gambette, Vincent Berry and Christophe Paul, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-02441-2_26">The structure of level-k phylogenetic networks</a>, LNCS 5577 (2009) 289-300.
%H A307185 Philippe Gambette, <a href="http://igm.univ-mlv.fr/~gambette/ProgGenerators.php">Generators - Building level-k generators</a>.
%H A307185 Philippe Gambette, <a href="http://igm.univ-mlv.fr/~gambette/ProgramGenerators/Lev5Gen.zip">Compressed list of all level-k generators for k < 6</a> (DOT format).
%H A307185 Tyler Satchel Orden, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22638092">Level-6 generators of phylogenetic networks: enumeration code, canonical-form lists and the generator files</a>, Zenodo, 2026 (the generator files are attached to the GitHub release linked from the record).
%K A307185 nonn,hard,more,changed
